Package: GLAMMGoF
Title: Resampling-Based Predictive Validation for Generalized Linear and Generalized Additive Models
Date: 2026-08-27
URL: https://github.com/colinpshea/glammgof
Version: 1.4.4
Authors@R: 
    person("Colin", "Shea", , "colin.shea@myfwc.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2906-250X"))
Description: Provides resampling-based predictive validation for generalized linear and generalized additive models (with or without random effects) fitted using packages such as 'glmmTMB', 'mgcv', 'stats', 'lme4', and 'MASS'. Predictive performance is assessed via repeated random holdout (Monte Carlo cross-validation) or bootstrap resampling with out-of-bag evaluation, generating sampling distributions of in-sample and out-of-sample metrics. Supported metrics include relative root mean squared error, relative mean absolute error, relative median absolute error, and relative bias for continuous or integer responses, and AUC, Brier score, and log loss for binary responses. Predictions are population-level by default; conditional and bias-adjusted predictions are also supported. Bias adjustment addresses the underestimation of the arithmetic mean arising from Jensen's inequality when back-transforming to the response scale, via analytical corrections for log-link and log-normal models. A parametric bootstrap function generates response-scale predictions with associated uncertainty intervals, with optional bias adjustment for Jensen's inequality. 
